 the function is continuous.\n\nThe function is discontinuous at $x=1.$ To see this, we note that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)=2\\ne 3={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x).\n$$\n\n \n\nWe conclude that the intermediate value theorem can be applied to the function $f(x)$ only on closed intervals that do not contain the point $x=1.$ \n\nFrom the given options, only the interval $[-2,0]$ is allowed.  The intervals $(1,3]$ and $[-2,1)$ are not closed, $[-2,1]$ and $[0,3]$ contain the point $x=1.$" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345031 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345032 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345033 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345034 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186345035 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1041 "selection" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1104 #edb/ref 17592186345031 13194139535345 true] [17592186345030 1110 #uuid "6057ac87-2a36-51ab-a6bc-c8d90498e45f" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345031 1034 "[-2,0]" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535345 true] [17592186345031 1111 #uuid "265faa65-e740-5f6a-adaf-a25daec9852f" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345032 1034 "[-2,1]" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535345 true] [17592186345032 1111 #uuid "344c5f03-f255-5fdd-9978-57b07397eecb" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345033 1034 "(1,3]" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535345 true] [17592186345033 1111 #uuid "7da63e35-551e-597e-8680-25e779f087cb" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345034 1034 "[0,3]" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535345 true] [17592186345034 1111 #uuid "8eaa55f4-8be3-5d67-b223-84127e46ec87" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345035 1034 "[-2,1)" 13194139535345 true] [17592186345035 110